This extension adds Marvel's Spider-Man 2 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Overstrike installed automatically.[/summary]

Overstrike will be installed automatically.
[size=3][b]This extension will automatically download and install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/marvelsspiderman2/mods/1]Overstrike[/url].
This extension optionally uses the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/409]Steamkit[/url] extension. Vortex will send you a notification with a button to download it. It is needed only on the Steam version.
[b]You must enable mods in Overstrike to install them to the game files! A notification will be shown after mod deployment to run Overstrike.[/b][/b][/size]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Overstrike mods with an "overstrike.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Overstrike mods with a ".smpcmod", ".suit", ".suit_style", ".stage", ".modular" or ".script" file install to the "Mods Library" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][size=2]Automatically installs[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/818] [/url]Overstrike. You must run Overstrike to install mods into the game data archives. [/size][/*]
[*][size=2]You can do a TOC reset (necessary after an update) - using the button in the folder icon on the Mods toolbar. If you are using Steam version, Vortex will also attempt to verify only the "toc" file from Steam automatically.[/size][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Marvel's Spider-Man 2 mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Overstrike:

Recognised when the archive contains a "overstrike.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Overstrike Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".smpcmod", ".suit", ".suit_style", ".stage", ".modular" or ".script" file.

  Installs to: "Mods Library"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

[b]🤝 Credits:[/b]
[list]
[*]Credit to [url=https://next.nexusmods.com/profile/Nagev/about-me]Nagev[/url] (Nexus Mods Vortex Developer) for his support on helping me learn to make Vortex extensions, and being patient when I break things :)[/*]
[/list]

[b][color=#ffff00][size=4]NOTICE for Overstrike regarding game updates:[/size][/color]
[/b][size=2]﻿If the game updates, your 'toc.BAK' file needs to be updated or it will cause problems/crashes. Do a "toc reset":[/size]
[size=2]  ﻿1) Delete 'toc' and 'toc.BAK' from game's folder;[/size]
[size=2]  ﻿2) Verify game files through Steam or EGS — that will download fresh 'toc';[/size]
[size=2]  ﻿3) Install mods in Overstrike — that'll copy fresh 'toc' into 'toc.BAK'.[/size]
